course: dictionary
lesson: 4020
title: Breaking down a hard word
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A long word can look scary, but you can often break it into smaller parts. Gastroenteritis has three parts: gastro means stomach, entero means gut, and -itis means swollen or sore.
explain: Put the parts together and you get a sore, swollen stomach and gut. The dictionary says that is exactly what this illness is.
explain: Now read the context. «A tummy bug, gastroenteritis, is an infection of the stomach and gut, often by norovirus» has a comma after tummy bug, which tells you the two names mean the same thing.
explain: The second sentence, «Gastroenteritis is an infection of the stomach and gut, usually by a virus such as norovirus, and the body clears it in a few days», shows it is an illness that gets better by itself.
fact: Gastroenteritis means an illness where the stomach and gut become sore and swollen.
fact: It is often called a «tummy bug» or «stomach flu».
fact: Its signs are sickness, diarrhoea (runny poo) and tummy pain.
fact: It is usually caused by a virus, such as norovirus, or by bacteria.
fact: It spreads easily, so wash your hands with soap after the toilet and before eating.
exercise: «Gastroenteritis is an infection of the stomach and gut, usually by a virus such as norovirus.» What does gastroenteritis mean? | A cut on the hand that bleeds | *An illness where the stomach and gut get sore and swollen | A broken bone in the leg | A cold that makes you sneeze
exercise: Gastro means stomach and entero means gut. Which part of the word means sore or swollen? | entero | *-itis | gastro | norovirus
exercise: Which of these is a common name for gastroenteritis? | *Tummy bug | Sunburn | Hay fever | Headache
test: «Being sick and having diarrhoea is your body throwing the germs out.» What does this tell you about gastroenteritis? | Your heart has stopped | *Your body is trying to get rid of the germs | Your bones are growing | Your eyes need glasses
test: Why should you wash your hands with soap before eating? | *Because gastroenteritis spreads easily | To make your hands smell nice | Because soap is a kind of food | To stop your hair getting wet
exam: Under the UK school rule, how long should a child with gastroenteritis stay off school after the last sickness or diarrhoea? | *48 hours | 24 hours | They can go straight back the same day | One week
